{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nWhen the completion verifier fails a close with \"insufficient evidence\" because the evidence search EXHAUSTED its step budget without refuting any criterion, the correct next action is mechanical: run it again. The verdict cache (Gerrit 1796) banks per-criterion PASSes at finalize even on overall FAIL, so a re-run seeds the credited criteria and spends its whole budget on the formerly-insufficient ones. This was demonstrated live (2026-08-14, ticket deadbeat-warlike-ostrich / 8d74): first close FAILed on exhaustion; an identical re-run closed clean with zero operator-added evidence. Operator ruling: bounded-search exhaustion is the gate's problem to resolve, not the operator's — the gate should auto-resume instead of demanding a human retype the same command.\n\n## Mechanism (maps to existing callables only)\nA resumption is a WHOLE-VERIFIER RE-RUN — exactly what the manual 8d74 re-close did — not a partial continuation. No new verification entry point:\n1. The resumption loop lives at the shared close-gate verification seam — the code that invokes `verify_completion` and inspects its verdict (gate dispatch / CompletionAgentStep caller side) — NOT in the CLI-only close path, so CLI, MCP, and library closes all get it. Executor confirms the exact seam (candidates: the gate_dispatch step that close_precheck's verdict inspection consumes) before coding, and records it in a ticket comment.\n2. Classification: a FAIL qualifies for auto-resume ONLY when (a) at least one criterion is insufficient-evidence/exhausted, and (b) NO criterion was REFUTED (affirmative evidence the work was not done). Any refutation → fail fast, no resume (current behavior). Classification comes from the per-criterion verdict statuses the verifier already returns (completion_failures.py taxonomy); no new telemetry.\n3. On qualification: re-invoke `verify_completion` with the same args/ref. The verdict cache seeds credited PASSes (existing behavior, no change needed); the fresh budget concentrates on remaining criteria (budget derivation unchanged — `verify_step_floor` stays parameterized on the total criteria count; concentration is emergent from cache hits consuming ~0 steps, as observed in the 8d74 live run).\n4. Bounded: `verify.auto_resume_max` resumptions per close invocation, default 2, 0 disables. Each resumption logged to the ticket trail (comment or verdict metadata): attempt number, criteria credited-from-cache count, criteria remaining.\n5. Overall outcome: PASS on any attempt → close proceeds. Still exhausted after the bounded resumptions → the existing failure surface, with the message stating auto-resume was attempted N times (operator sees honest state).\n\n## Out of scope (split to child idea ticket)\nSearch-frontier handoff (steering a resumption away from already-searched places / toward where credited evidence was found) requires an argument-level tool-call transcript the verifier telemetry does not currently carry. That capability question — and the extractor design on top of it — is a separate idea ticket linked discovered_from this one; THIS ticket's resumption passes no frontier and needs no fallback (cache seeding alone proved sufficient live).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Auto-resume triggers only on exhaustion-without-refutation: unit tests cover (a) exhausted+no-refutation → resumes; (b) any refuted criterion → fails fast with no resume; (c) plain PASS → no resume.\n- [ ] Resumption re-invokes the existing `verify_completion` entry (asserted via call-count on the real seam), with the same ref binding (`--ref` closes resume against the same pinned ref).\n- [ ] Bounded by `verify.auto_resume_max` (default 2, 0 disables; config-registry regenerated); attempts beyond the bound surface the existing failure with an attempts-count message (tested).\n- [ ] Resumption trail recorded per attempt (attempt number, cache-credited count, remaining count) and visible on the ticket or in the close output (tested).\n- [ ] The loop sits at the shared gate seam: an MCP-or-library-path close exercises it in a test, not only the CLI path.\n- [ ] Child idea ticket for frontier handoff created + linked discovered_from this ticket before this ticket closes.\n- [ ] `make lint` / `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786766844228406001,"uuid":"57bbbb6c-3336-4b3b-8099-33163e558ab8"}